  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine Farmers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFC expects the Project to contribute to global food security by supporting grain origination in Ukraine and exporting to, among other regions, developing countries in Africa, Asia, and the Middle East. The Project will also support jobs and the livelihoods of Ukrainian farmers and generate value addition and employment to the Ukrainian economy. Beyond the Project, IFC anticipates that its financing will contribute to promoting resilience in Ukraines agribusiness sector.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFC will partially guarantee the receivables of Soufflet Agro Ukraine CJSC from farmers and grain buyers and provide liquidity support for the operations of InVivo Group direct and/or indirect subsidiaries in Ukraine (Project). The Project is expected to be supported by Blended Finance contributors under the Economic Resilience Action (ERA) Program for Ukraine  the Netherlands, as described in the Blended Finance Section.</narrative>
  </description>
